#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "gitformat-loose(5)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:7
msgid "gitformat-loose - Git loose object format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:10
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:13
msgid "$GIT_DIR/objects/[0-9a-f][0-9a-f]/*"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:15
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:19
msgid ""
"Loose objects are how Git stores individual objects, where every object is "
"written as a separate file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Over the lifetime of a repository, objects are usually written as loose "
"objects initially.  Eventually, these loose objects will be compacted into "
"packfiles via repository maintenance to improve disk space usage and speed "
"up the lookup of these objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:25
#, no-wrap
msgid "Loose objects"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:31
msgid ""
"Each loose object contains a prefix, followed immediately by the data of the "
"object.  The prefix contains `<type> <size>\\0`.  `<type>` is one of `blob`, "
"`tree`, `commit`, or `tag` and `size` is the size of the data (without the "
"prefix) as a decimal integer expressed in ASCII."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:35
msgid ""
"The entire contents, prefix and data concatenated, is then compressed with "
"zlib and the compressed data is stored in the file.  The object ID of the "
"object is the SHA-1 or SHA-256 (as appropriate) hash of the uncompressed "
"data."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:41
msgid ""
"The file for the loose object is stored under the `objects` directory, with "
"the first two hex characters of the object ID being the directory and the "
"remaining characters being the file name.  This is done to shard the data "
"and avoid too many files being in one directory, since some file systems "
"perform poorly with many items in a directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:47
msgid ""
"As an example, the empty tree contains the data (when uncompressed) `tree "
"0\\0` and, in a SHA-256 repository, would have the object ID "
"`6ef19b41225c5369f1c104d45d8d85efa9b057b53b14b4b9b939dd74decc5321` and would "
"be stored under `$GIT_DIR/objects/6e/"
"f19b41225c5369f1c104d45d8d85efa9b057b53b14b4b9b939dd74decc5321`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/gitformat-loose.adoc:50
msgid ""
"Similarly, a blob containing the contents `abc` would have the uncompressed "
"data of `blob 3\\0abc`."
msgstr ""

